=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play dns/failed-reload ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: dns/failed-reload$
# web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 26.04; /etc/resolv.conf links$
# to systemd-resolved's stub, and eth0 has 192.0.2.1 and$
# example.net from DHCP. hardn.yml lists 192.0.2.54,$
# 2001:db8::54. Its next reload of systemd-resolved loads$
# nothing new, so a change fails and is rolled back.$
$
# DNS Configuration ############################################$
$
  Current DNS Configuration ------------------------------------$
$
   -  DNS Implementation   systemd-resolved$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.1 (eth0)$
   -  Search Domains       example.net (eth0)$
$
  Configured Nameservers ---------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameserver 1         192.0.2.54$
   -  Nameserver 2         2001:db8::54$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Configure DNS        Apply nameserver settings from con...$
   2) Add nameserver       Add a new DNS server to configuration$
   3) Remove nameserver    Remove a DNS server from configura...$
   4) Use Cloudflare DNS   Set nameservers to 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   5) Use Google DNS       Set nameservers to 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4$
   6) Use Quad9 DNS        Set nameservers to 9.9.9.9, 149.11...$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-6 or q]: 1$
$
# Configure DNS ################################################$
$
  DNS Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54$
   -  Search Domains       example.net (eth0)$
  [ ] eth0 still uses its own nameserver 192.0.2.1$
$
   -  Set the nameservers$
      /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,5 @@$
      +# Written by hardn: the system DNS servers for$
      | systemd-resolved.$
      +# An empty assignment resets the list that earlier files$
      | built.$
      +[Resolve]$
      +DNS=$
      +DNS=192.0.2.54 2001:db8::54$
      $ systemctl try-reload-or-restart systemd-resolved.service$
$
  Configure DNS? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [ ] Set the nameservers  Failed DNS_NOT_EFFECTIVE$
$
# Operation Failed$
# Reloading systemd-resolved had no effect$
$
  [ ] Set the nameservers  Rolled back$
$
  Check the log file at /var/log/hardn.log for details$
  Run resolvectl dns to see the servers in use.$
$
# DNS Configuration ############################################$
$
  Current DNS Configuration ------------------------------------$
$
   -  DNS Implementation   systemd-resolved$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.1 (eth0)$
   -  Search Domains       example.net (eth0)$
$
  Configured Nameservers ---------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameserver 1         192.0.2.54$
   -  Nameserver 2         2001:db8::54$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Configure DNS        Apply nameserver settings from con...$
   2) Add nameserver       Add a new DNS server to configuration$
   3) Remove nameserver    Remove a DNS server from configura...$
   4) Use Cloudflare DNS   Set nameservers to 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   5) Use Google DNS       Set nameservers to 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4$
   6) Use Quad9 DNS        Set nameservers to 9.9.9.9, 149.11...$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-6 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: dns/failed-reload$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Failed: Set the nameservers$
      /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d,$
      | /etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/zz-hardn.conf$
      $ systemctl try-reload-or-restart systemd-resolved.service$
      $ systemctl reload-or-restart systemd-resolved.service$
$

